From bc3540eb788f573f9cdf562f983e4f1fe77db8cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 20:40:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 24/38] feat(qwen3-tts): re-port streaming worker to v0.9.0
 native streaming API
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Re-port of the v0.8.0 qwen3_tts_streaming_worker (10b338d) onto the v0.9.0
runtime, M1 milestone. Zero cpp/runtime/ changes.

Protocol (voxedge consumer contract) is byte-for-byte compatible:
ready / chunk(base64 PCM_S16LE, is_final) / done / error events, request_id+id,
pool saturation error with status 4429, EDGE_LLM_TTS_MAX_CONCURRENT env.

Internals moved to the v0.9.0 API:
- handleAudioGeneration(vector<TalkerGenerationRequest>) with messages-wrapped
  assistant text (the only text entry point in 0.9.0).
- Native TalkerGenerationRequest::streamingChunkFrames + onChunkReady(codes,
  isFinal) replaces the old runtime-side chunk surgery. Uniform chunk size =
  first_chunk_frames (chunk_frames accepted, folded into uniform chunking).
- Code2Wav vocoding stays worker-side (per-slot stateless Code2WavRunner,
  optional EDGE_LLM_TTS_ASYNC_VOCODE overlap thread, unchanged).
- Waveform dtype handling: 0.9.0 Code2Wav returns the engine's output dtype
  (FP16 on Jetson) — convert per-dtype instead of assuming FP32.

M1 limitations (by design, spec docs/specs/edgellm-v090-tts-re-port.md):
- cancel: no runtime cancel mechanism in 0.9.0 yet (M3). cancel lines get
  cancel_ack{tripped:false, error:cancel_not_supported_yet}.
- every slot uses the path-based ctor (shared-engine ctor is M3);
  max_slots=1 is the validated config.
- language / speaker_embedding_b64 accepted-and-warned (runtime support M2).

slotPool.h is a verbatim carry-over of the v0.8.0 cpp/runtime/slotPool.h,
parked under examples/omni/ to keep cpp/runtime/ untouched in M1.

